class Solution {
    public double fractionalKnapsack(int[] val, int[] wt, long cap) {
        int n = val.length;
        boolean[] used = new boolean[n];
        long remaining = cap;
        double answer = 0.0;

        while (remaining > 0) {
            int best = -1;
            double bestRatio = -1.0;

            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
                if (!used[i] && wt[i] > 0) {
                    double ratio = (double) val[i] / wt[i];
                    if (ratio > bestRatio) {
                        bestRatio = ratio;
                        best = i;
                    }
                }
            }

            if (best == -1) {
                break;
            }

            used[best] = true;
            long taken = Math.min(remaining, (long) wt[best]);
            answer += taken * bestRatio;
            remaining -= taken;
        }

        return answer;
    }
}
```

Time complexity: `O(n^2)` due to scanning all remaining items on every round.
Space complexity: `O(n)` for the used markers. The input arrays stay unchanged.

